2. AgentConfig::build_agent applies that list at src/agent_builder.rs:907-908 via tools.retain(...).
3. It then pushes the sub-agent tool unconditionally at :951, after the filter — and that file's own comment at :880 says out loud that disallowed_tools "couldn't catch" sub_agent/shared_state because "they were added after filtering".
4. build_sub_agent_tool hands the child a raw BashTool (`src/tools.rs:1388) with no reference to disallowed_tools`.

So bash is genuinely removed from the top-level set, sub_agent survives, and the surviving sub_agent builds its own shell — command execution is still reachable in one call. That is verbatim the "fence with a gate in it" the new const's doc claims to close.

